1
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:32,400
An Ancient Prophecy Foretold. A Scientific Discovery Revealed.

2
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:58,800
2012 Doomsday is a action, adventure, fantasy film directed by Nick Everhart.

3
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:25,200
On December 21, 2012 four strangers on a journey of faith are
drawn to an ancient temple in the heart of Mexico.

4
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:51,600
For the Mayans it is the last recorded day.

5
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:18,000
For NASA scientists it is a cataclysmic polar shift.

6
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:44,400
For the rest of us, it is Doomsday.

7
00:24:04,799 --> 00:24:10,799
Lloyd, played by Cliff DeYoung.

8
00:27:31,200 --> 00:27:37,200
Dr. Frank Richards, played by Dale Midkiff.

9
00:30:57,600 --> 00:31:03,600
Susan, played by Ami Dolenz.

10
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:30,000
Sarah, played by Danae Nason.

11
00:37:50,400 --> 00:37:56,400
Alex, played by Joshua Lee.

12
00:41:16,800 --> 00:41:22,800
Wakanna, played by Sara Tomko.

13
00:44:43,200 --> 00:44:49,200
Doomsday is a 2008 science fiction action film
written and directed by Neil Marshall.

14
00:48:09,599 --> 00:48:15,599
The film takes place in the future in Scotland, which has
been quarantined because of a deadly virus.

15
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:42,000
When the virus is found in London, political leaders send a team led by Major
Eden Sinclair (Rhona Mitra) to Scotland to find a possible cure.

16
00:55:02,400 --> 00:55:08,400
Sinclair's team runs into two types of survivors: marauders and
survivors styling themselves after medieval knights.

17
00:58:28,800 --> 00:58:34,800
Doomsday was conceived by Marshall based on the idea of
futuristic soldiers facing medieval knights.

18
01:01:55,200 --> 01:02:01,200
In producing the film, he drew inspiration from various movies,
including Mad Max, Escape from New York and 28 Days Later.

19
01:05:21,599 --> 01:05:27,599
Marshall had a budget three times the size of his previous two films, The Descent and Dog
Soldiers, and the director filmed the larger-scale Doomsday in Scotland and South Africa.

20
01:08:48,000 --> 01:08:54,000
The film was released in the United States and Canada on 14
March 2008 and in the United Kingdom on 9 May 2008.

21
01:12:14,400 --> 01:12:20,400
It received mixed reviews from critics, who praised the casting, pacing, narrative, and homage to previous
films, but criticized the plot holes, character development, confusing editing, and excessive gore.

22
01:15:40,800 --> 01:15:46,800
The film grossed $22 million worldwide, making it a box office bomb.

23
01:19:07,199 --> 01:19:13,199
The film explores themes of mexico, faith,
dystopia, end of the world, apocalypse.

24
01:22:33,600 --> 01:22:39,600
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
